title: Payers › Workflow Builder › Configure a step
route: /payers/summit?tab=builder
intro: Selecting a step opens its settings on the right, with only the controls that step needs. The top is the same for every step; the middle depends on the kind of step (the family diagrams below); the bottom is where it goes next and what keeps it safe. Advanced settings stay folded.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Click a step on the canvas\nor focus it and press Enter"
screen hd "Settings header\nStep icon, its name, a dot and a word: Live, Demo simulation or Not configured\nA line saying what is real and what is simulated\n'Close the step settings'"
decision d1 "Does the step have a problem?"
screen iss "Red or ochre lines at the top\n'Needs fixing: ...' or 'Check: ...' for this step"
screen com "Common controls\n'Title'\n'How it runs': Automatic, Manual or Agent-assisted\nFold 'Description and instructions' (short description, instructions for the people who run it)"
screen typ "Controls for this kind of step\nEach one has its own diagram"
screen nxt "'Next steps'\nOne list per exit, e.g. 'When: Yes' and 'When: No'\nThe steps that can be reached, or 'Not connected'"
click c1 "Pick a step in a 'Next steps' list"
process p1 "A line is drawn from that exit to the step, or removed for 'Not connected'\nAnnounced: 'Connected A to B'"
screen saf "'Completion and safeguards'\n'Completion criteria', 'A person approves first', 'If the step fails',\n'Retries before manual review' when the choice is 'Retry, then manual review'"
decision d2 "Does the step reach out to a payer, a fax line or another system?"
process p2 "'A person approves first' is on and cannot be turned off\n'Steps that reach the payer always need a person's approval.'"
process p3 "The switch is free to change"
click c2 "Open 'Advanced'"
screen adv "'Stage in New Case' (Intake, Eligibility & Benefits, Clinical documentation, Authorization preparation, Review & submit)\nOther advanced fields for the step, and the step id"
click c3 "Click 'Duplicate' or 'Delete' at the foot of the panel"
process p4 "A copy is made 48 px away, or the step and its lines are removed\nStart has neither button: 'Every workflow has one Start.'"
process p5 "Every edit is held in the builder and marked 'Unsaved changes'\nNothing reaches the store until 'Save draft'"
decision d3 "Is the workflow archived?"
process p6 "Every control is dimmed: archived workflows are read only"
end e1 "The step is configured in the draft"
goto g1 "Continues in: Payers › Workflow Builder › Save a draft and publish"

s1 --> hd --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| iss --> com
d1 -->|No| com
com --> typ --> nxt --> c1 --> p1 --> saf
saf --> d2
d2 -->|Yes| p2 --> c2
d2 -->|No| p3 --> c2
c2 --> adv --> c3 --> p4 --> p5
hd --> d3
d3 -->|Yes| p6
d3 -->|No| com
p5 --> e1 --> g1
